    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\r\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span><span class=\"time\">45 min</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip accent\">Pattern primer</span><span class=\"chip\">XOR</span><span class=\"chip\">Bitmask</span>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <h1>Bit manipulation</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">Six idioms cover almost every interview bit question: XOR cancels pairs, <code>n &amp; (n-1)</code> drops the lowest set bit, <code>x &amp; -x</code> keeps it, a mask is a set, shifts move bits, and a carry is just <code>(a &amp; b) &lt;&lt; 1</code>. You already write all of them in driver code; here they become interview answers.</p>\r\n  <p class=\"small prereq\"><b>Go deeper:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-bitmask-dp\">Bitmask DP</a>.</p>\r\n"
  },
